1
00:00:02,711 --> 00:00:05,130
Ross, when's this
comet thing start?

2
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:08,091
Well, technically,
it started seven
billion years ago...

3
00:00:08,091 --> 00:00:09,259
No, no!
Whoa!

4
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:11,720
Okay, okay,
fine, I'll stop.

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:13,012
No teaching, okay?

6
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:15,182
We'll just watch
the pretty lights

7
00:00:15,182 --> 00:00:16,934
streaking across the sky.

8
00:00:16,934 --> 00:00:18,519
Okay?
Okay.

9
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:21,313
Whose official name
is Bapstein-King...

10
00:00:21,313 --> 00:00:24,817
Oh, come on!
Okay, okay!

11
00:00:24,817 --> 00:00:26,735
There it is!

12
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:28,570
Oh, look at that.

13
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:31,907
Isn't Mother Nature amazing?

14
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:35,452
That's a plane.

15
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:36,745
Well, all right

16
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:39,707
1,700 bags of peanuts
flying that high

17
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:42,083
that's pretty amazing, too.

18
00:00:44,085 --> 00:00:45,921
Hey, I wonder if you can see
my apartment from up here. 

19
00:00:45,921 --> 00:00:49,008
Oh, no, you can't.

20
00:00:49,008 --> 00:00:50,009
What?

21
00:00:50,009 --> 00:00:52,011
I don't... I don't know.

22
00:00:52,011 --> 00:00:55,639
Wow, look at
all those stars.

23
00:00:55,639 --> 00:00:58,058
Infinite space.

24
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,977
Really... really makes
you wonder, doesn't it?

25
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:01,144
Yeah.

26
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:02,354
You know what else
makes you wonder?

27
00:01:02,354 --> 00:01:03,438
Huh?

28
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:06,149
Check out the rack
on this chick!

29
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:20,789
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪ 

30
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:23,208
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

31
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:24,960
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

32
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:29,798
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

33
00:01:29,798 --> 00:01:33,092
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

34
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:35,387
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

35
00:01:35,387 --> 00:01:39,349
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

36
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:45,064
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

37
00:01:51,570 --> 00:01:53,321
Okay, we've been out here
for two hours

38
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:55,198
and we haven't seen
any stupid comets.

39
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:56,909
Can we go now?

40
00:01:56,909 --> 00:02:00,746
I mean, Chandler's
getting chilly.

41
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:06,835
No, I'm n-not.

42
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:10,255
Then why are you wearing
Monica's jacket?

43
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:14,175
Because it's flattering.

44
00:02:14,175 --> 00:02:15,844
Come on, Monica,
come on, Monica.

45
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:17,512
Yeah, you
know what?

46
00:02:17,512 --> 00:02:19,807
I think we're going to take off.
We rented a movie.

47
00:02:19,807 --> 00:02:21,600
Oh, I won't say no to a movie.

48
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:24,394
Oh, Pheebs, we just actually
kind of wanted to be alone.

49
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:26,021
Shh. Get me out of here.
Oh, okay.

50
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:31,944
Hey, Ross...
What?

51
00:02:31,944 --> 00:02:33,737
Come here, check this out.
What, is it the comet?

52
00:02:33,737 --> 00:02:35,030
No, no... look,

53
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:38,784
there's a bug stuck
in tar right here.

54
00:02:38,784 --> 00:02:40,327
Joey, I can't believe it.

55
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:43,162
I bring you here to see
the Bapstein-King Comet

56
00:02:43,162 --> 00:02:45,666
one of nature's most
spectacular phenomena

57
00:02:45,666 --> 00:02:48,293
and all you care about
are bugs stuck in tar

58
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:50,420
and some woman.

59
00:02:52,464 --> 00:02:55,592
You know,
there's two women, dude.

60
00:02:56,885 --> 00:03:00,014
Show me where?

61
00:03:00,014 --> 00:03:01,765
Right up here.

62
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:08,981
Joey, where's the pipe

63
00:03:08,981 --> 00:03:10,649
that was holding
the door open?

64
00:03:10,649 --> 00:03:13,027
I don't know.

65
00:03:20,784 --> 00:03:23,328
Yeah, I do.

66
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,331
Joey!

67
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:27,875
What? All right...
Hey, don't look at me.

68
00:03:27,875 --> 00:03:29,459
You're the one who
wanted to come up here

69
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:33,172
and look for some stupid...
Burger King Comet!

70
00:03:33,172 --> 00:03:36,133
It's called
the Bapstein-King Comet, okay?

71
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,592
Oh...
Hey, hey!

72
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:40,721
Bapstein was a very
well-respected astronomer...

73
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:42,263
No-no! No!

74
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:44,307
No!

75
00:03:52,107 --> 00:03:53,525
( whispering ):
Monica...

76
00:03:53,525 --> 00:03:58,072
( whispering ):
She's sleeping.

77
00:03:58,072 --> 00:04:00,532
I know, just quick question.
Quick question.

78
00:04:00,532 --> 00:04:02,492
Which one was
Deep Impact

79
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:05,120
and which one
was Armageddon?

80
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:11,126
Deep Impact was the one
with Robert Duvall.

81
00:04:11,126 --> 00:04:13,170
Armageddon is what's
going to happen to you

82
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:14,713
if you wake me up.

83
00:04:14,713 --> 00:04:19,634
Sorry, I just...
can't sleep.

84
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:21,011
Ooh!

85
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:23,847
( groans )

86
00:04:23,847 --> 00:04:25,140
Where is that book
that you were reading

87
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:28,102
with the two women
who were ice-skating

88
00:04:28,102 --> 00:04:30,938
and wearing those hats
with the flowers on it?

89
00:04:30,938 --> 00:04:33,272
Because every time I look
at that cover, I'm like...

90
00:04:33,272 --> 00:04:34,858
( snoring noises )

91
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:39,738
It is in the living room,
where there is also a light.

92
00:04:39,738 --> 00:04:41,990
And no one will kick you
in the shin.

93
00:04:43,075 --> 00:04:44,076
What?

94
00:04:44,076 --> 00:04:46,286
Ow!

95
00:04:51,416 --> 00:04:56,838
( beeping )

96
00:04:56,838 --> 00:05:00,884
Please don't be a spaceship.
Please don't be a spaceship.

97
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:08,183
( beeping continues )

98
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:11,145
Oh, thank God.

99
00:05:27,911 --> 00:05:30,580
( beeping )

100
00:05:38,172 --> 00:05:40,090
( grunts )

101
00:05:41,382 --> 00:05:43,510
( beeping )

102
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:44,970
How could you be beeping?

103
00:05:44,970 --> 00:05:46,888
I just disconnected you!

104
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:48,015
I took out your battery!

105
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:49,224
( beeps )
How can--

106
00:05:49,224 --> 00:05:51,350
Don't interrupt me!

107
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:54,146
Rachel!

108
00:05:54,146 --> 00:05:55,730
Monica!

109
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:56,940
Come on!

110
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:02,612
I can't believe this!

111
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:04,114
All right, well, you know.

112
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:05,866
I guess we know what we
have to do to get down.

113
00:06:05,866 --> 00:06:06,950
Yeah...

114
00:06:06,950 --> 00:06:09,119
I guess we don't have a choice.

115
00:06:10,037 --> 00:06:13,290
Help us!
Please, help us!

116
00:06:13,290 --> 00:06:17,878
We're stuck up on the roof
and we can't get down!

117
00:06:19,338 --> 00:06:21,923
Ross...

118
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:25,510
I was thinking we'd just go down
the fire escape.

119
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:28,805
I know, I wasn't finished.

120
00:06:31,683 --> 00:06:34,393
But don't worry!

121
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:38,481
We're going to go down
the fire escape!

122
00:06:45,239 --> 00:06:47,615
( loud clattering )

123
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:50,327
Shh!

124
00:06:53,747 --> 00:06:56,041
I'm sorry. I thought maybe
I'd make some warm milk

125
00:06:56,041 --> 00:06:57,625
and it would help me sleep.

126
00:06:57,625 --> 00:06:59,169
With a wok?

127
00:07:00,712 --> 00:07:02,463
I thought you were going to read
my boring book

128
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:03,590
to put you to sleep?

129
00:07:03,590 --> 00:07:06,343
It got interesting.

130
00:07:06,343 --> 00:07:08,511
Damn you, Oprah!

131
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:11,056
Here, let me
make the milk.

132
00:07:11,056 --> 00:07:12,307
I'm up anyway.

133
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:13,474
Hey, you know
what we could do,

134
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:15,185
you know, now
that we're up?

135
00:07:15,185 --> 00:07:18,063
We could just, like,
talk to each other
all night long.

136
00:07:18,063 --> 00:07:19,731
You know, like we did
when we were first going out.

137
00:07:19,731 --> 00:07:20,899
It'd be fun.

138
00:07:20,899 --> 00:07:22,817
Okay, that does sound fun.
Yeah.

139
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:24,361
So, how bummed were you

140
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:26,487
when the second sister died,
huh?

141
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:28,656
The second sister dies?!

142
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:37,040
No...

143
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,834
No, I-I was, I was talking
about the book I was reading.

144
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:41,044
The second sister dies

145
00:07:41,044 --> 00:07:44,131
in Archie and Jughead
Double Digest?

146
00:07:45,799 --> 00:07:47,467
That's correct.

147
00:07:53,932 --> 00:07:55,600
You want to go
in the bedroom?

148
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,144
A little more
comfortable.

149
00:07:57,144 --> 00:07:58,603
Sure.
Okay.

150
00:08:00,272 --> 00:08:01,564
Oh, wait, um...

151
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:03,817
Did you send those
contracts to Milan?

152
00:08:03,817 --> 00:08:06,027
If this is your idea
of sexy talk...

153
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:07,321
( chuckles )

154
00:08:07,321 --> 00:08:08,488
No, seriously.

155
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:09,990
You know the contracts
I gave you?

156
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:12,242
did you overnight them?
What contracts?

157
00:08:12,242 --> 00:08:14,786
Okay, please tell me this
is just one of your jokes

158
00:08:14,786 --> 00:08:16,413
that you do
that I don't get.

159
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:17,414
Like what?

160
00:08:17,414 --> 00:08:18,748
You know, like the thing

161
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:20,292
when you put the phone
in your pants?

162
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:22,461
( laughs )

163
00:08:22,461 --> 00:08:23,462
Tag, I'm serious.

164
00:08:23,462 --> 00:08:24,963
This isn't funny.

165
00:08:24,963 --> 00:08:27,757
Those contracts absolutely
had to go out today.

166
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:30,260
Rach, I'm sorry, but you
didn't give me any contracts.

167
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:32,887
Yes, I did and I put
a little Post-it on it

168
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:35,056
that said, "Must go out today"

169
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:37,351
and I underlined
"today" three times

170
00:08:37,351 --> 00:08:39,269
and then I put a little heart
in the corner

171
00:08:39,269 --> 00:08:42,105
'cause I didn't want to seem
too bossy.

172
00:08:42,105 --> 00:08:44,065
I'm telling you,
you never gave them to me.

173
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,360
You know what, Tag,
if we went down to the office

174
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:49,321
you would see those contracts
sitting on your desk.

175
00:08:49,321 --> 00:08:51,365
No, I would see you
looking embarrassed

176
00:08:51,365 --> 00:08:53,450
because they are not on my desk.

177
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:55,243
Or maybe you would see me
looking embarrassed

178
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:58,497
because you are talking
on the phone with your crotch.

179
00:08:58,497 --> 00:09:01,041
Look, do you want to go down
to the office right now?

180
00:09:01,041 --> 00:09:02,417
No, come on, it's late.

181
00:09:02,417 --> 00:09:05,086
We're not going to go down
to the office.

182
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:07,588
Yeah, I understand.

183
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:09,341
I wouldn't want
to be proved wrong either.

184
00:09:09,341 --> 00:09:11,510
All right,
get your coat!

185
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:15,722
Oh! When did you unhook this?

186
00:09:15,722 --> 00:09:16,764
Nice work.

187
00:09:22,854 --> 00:09:24,814
( grunting )

188
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:26,983
It won't go down
any further, it's stuck.

189
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,568
( sighs )

190
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,820
Well, we're just
going to have to jump.

191
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,155
Yeah.

192
00:09:32,155 --> 00:09:34,074
Now, we're going to
have to make sure

193
00:09:34,074 --> 00:09:35,992
to land to the right

194
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:38,828
of that patch of ice, okay?

195
00:09:38,828 --> 00:09:42,416
Not hit the Dumpster
on the other side

196
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:44,792
and try to avoid
that-that...

197
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:48,046
weird brownish-red
stuff in the middle.

198
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:51,466
So, when you
get down there...

199
00:09:54,261 --> 00:09:56,679
you go up to the roof

200
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:59,266
and you let me in.

201
00:09:59,266 --> 00:10:01,642
Whoa, wait a minute,
I have to do it?

202
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:02,894
Yeah, oh, yeah.
You'll be fine.

203
00:10:02,894 --> 00:10:04,104
It'll be, uh...

204
00:10:04,104 --> 00:10:05,730
just like bungee
jumping, you know?

205
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:07,774
But instead of
bouncing back up

206
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:09,943
you... you won't.

207
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:15,407
But what if I smack my head
on the concrete?

208
00:10:15,407 --> 00:10:17,325
Well, I'm not going
to lie to you, Joey.

209
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:19,160
It's a possibility.

210
00:10:22,163 --> 00:10:23,206
I don't know, Ross.

211
00:10:23,206 --> 00:10:24,374
I tell you what

212
00:10:24,374 --> 00:10:25,875
let's flip to see
who does it, okay?

213
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:27,668
You call it in the air,
all right?

214
00:10:27,668 --> 00:10:28,711
Oh, all right.
Tails... 

215
00:10:28,711 --> 00:10:29,754
Ooh!

216
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:35,469
Can you... can you
see what it is?

217
00:10:35,469 --> 00:10:36,595
No.

218
00:10:36,595 --> 00:10:37,971
Okay, well, you
be careful.

219
00:10:37,971 --> 00:10:39,139
Wha... no-no, Ross.

220
00:10:39,139 --> 00:10:40,307
No, no... stop.

221
00:10:40,307 --> 00:10:41,808
I'm not jumping!
Well...

222
00:10:41,808 --> 00:10:43,893
Okay, look, I have
an audition tomorrow

223
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:45,770
and I can't go
if I break my leg.

224
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:47,188
Well, I'm not jumping.

225
00:10:47,188 --> 00:10:48,440
I have a son, okay?

226
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:50,609
He won't have a
father if I die.

227
00:10:50,609 --> 00:10:52,735
Well, all right,
so it looks like we're even.

228
00:10:57,824 --> 00:11:01,786
Okay, so this wire
is connected to this wire

229
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:03,622
which plugs into here.

230
00:11:03,622 --> 00:11:06,874
Okay, so to get the beeping
to stop,

231
00:11:06,874 --> 00:11:09,961
all I have to do...

232
00:11:20,597 --> 00:11:23,183
Well done, Pheebs.

233
00:11:23,183 --> 00:11:25,935
( rapid beeping )

234
00:11:27,187 --> 00:11:30,857
What do you want from me?!

235
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:35,820
Okay, here's your milk.

236
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:37,447
What do you want to talk about?

237
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:42,160
( slams door )
What? What?

238
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:44,245
Oh, were you sleeping,
sweetie?

239
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:47,165
I'm sorry... here.

240
00:11:52,212 --> 00:11:54,589
Okay, feel free to look,
but I'm telling you

241
00:11:54,589 --> 00:11:57,008
those contracts
are not on this desk.

242
00:11:57,008 --> 00:11:59,636
How could you possibly know?
Look at this mess, Tag.

243
00:11:59,636 --> 00:12:01,179
I mean, this is what
I'm talking about.

244
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:03,515
You have to be
more organized.

245
00:12:03,515 --> 00:12:05,600
You've got newspapers,
you've got magazines,

246
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:08,186
you've... oh!

247
00:12:08,186 --> 00:12:10,855
And who's this chippy?

248
00:12:10,855 --> 00:12:13,066
A little young for you, Tag,
but whatever.

249
00:12:13,066 --> 00:12:14,401
It's my sister?

250
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:18,196
Really? Very cute braces.

251
00:12:18,196 --> 00:12:19,947
Anyway,
you know what?

252
00:12:19,947 --> 00:12:22,534
The point is, Tag, start looking

253
00:12:22,534 --> 00:12:25,662
because you are going to find
those contracts on your desk.

254
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:28,789
So when do
you imagine

255
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:29,957
you gave them to me?

256
00:12:29,957 --> 00:12:31,501
In the morning
or in the afternoon?

257
00:12:31,501 --> 00:12:32,835
In the afternoon.

258
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:35,672
Mr. Zelner came into my office
after lunch

259
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:37,173
he put them on my desk

260
00:12:37,173 --> 00:12:39,593
and then I put a Post-it
on it...

261
00:12:41,553 --> 00:12:42,679
that said...

